# WeStartup — Cursor Project Rules

## Product

**WeStartup** — AI-powered platform where founders pressure-test startup ideas with a
challenging AI advisor, then leave with investor-ready documents as an interactive
analytics dashboard.

Tagline: *From idea to investor-ready in under an hour*

The AI advisor is **not a yes-man**: challenge weak assumptions, demand evidence,
probe viability/marketability, prepare founders for real investor meetings.

---

## Stack (locked)

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Framework | Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 |
| Components | shadcn/ui (customized — never ship default slate/zinc theme) |
| Auth + DB | Supabase (email/password + magic link + Google OAuth, Postgres) |
| Payments | **Razorpay only** (UPI, cards, netbanking, wallets) — no Stripe |
| AI | Vercel AI SDK; Gemini primary, Groq fallback via config |
| Charts | Recharts (structured JSON from model → client render) |
| Package manager | npm |
| Currency | INR (₹) for all pricing UI |

Backend logic lives in Next.js Route Handlers / Server Actions only.

---

## Build discipline

1. Build incrementally. Do **not** scaffold entire features at once.
2. Before each feature/step: ask clarifying questions; wait for answers or
   “proceed with best judgment.”
3. After clarifications: implement **only** that step. Preserve existing behavior.
4. Explain architectural decisions before major changes.
5. Production-ready TypeScript, strong typing, clear folder structure.

### Skill invocation (per feature, in order)

| Order | Skill | When |
|-------|-------|------|
| 1 | **refero** (`.cursor/skills/refero-design`) | Layout, IA, structure |
| 2 | **leon** (taste-skill under `.agents/skills`) | Color, type, spacing, design language |
| 3 | **animation** (emilkowalski skills) | Motion, transitions, micro-interactions |

Do **not** invoke all skills at project start — only when that concern is active.

---

## Visual identity — “Signal Teal” (hybrid, locked)

Refero-grounded: neutrals-first, no indigo/violet AI default, no cream+terracotta
editorial cliché. Hybrid: **light marketing** + **denser dark app chrome**.

### Palette

| Token | Hex | Role |
|-------|-----|------|
| `--canvas` | `#F5F7F9` | Marketing / light surfaces |
| `--ink` | `#0B1220` | Primary text (light), app chrome base |
| `--ink-elevated` | `#141C2B` | App elevated panels |
| `--ink-muted` | `#8B95A8` | Secondary text on dark |
| `--border-light` | `#D8DEE8` | Light borders |
| `--border-dark` | `#243044` | Dark borders |
| `--accent` | `#0F766E` | CTA, focus, chart primary (teal) |
| `--accent-hover` | `#0D9488` | Hover / active accent |
| `--accent-subtle` | `#CCFBF1` | Light accent wash |
| `--challenge` | `#B45309` | Advisor pushback / warnings (not celebration) |
| `--success` | `#047857` | Positive / confirmed |
| `--danger` | `#B91C1C` | Errors / destructive |

### Typography

- **UI + body:** Plus Jakarta Sans (`--font-sans`)
- **Marketing display / brand moments only:** Newsreader (`--font-display`)
- Do **not** use Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system-ui as primary brand fonts.
- Scale: Minor Third (~1.2). Denser in app chrome; more open on marketing.

### Layout / craft rules

- Brand “WeStartup” is hero-level on marketing — not nav-only.
- Default: **no cards**. Cards only for interactive containers.
- Prefer borders + spacing over multi-layer shadows / glow.
- Radius: 8–12px. No rounded-full pill clusters.
- Marketing first viewport: brand, one headline, one supporting line, one CTA group,
  one dominant visual — nothing else.
- Copy tone: restrained, professional; no emoji / exclamation-driven microcopy.

### Theme application

- `(marketing)`, `(auth)`, `(onboarding)`: light canvas + ink text.
- `(app)` chat/dashboard shell: dark ink chrome; charts/accents use teal.

---

## File structure

```
app/
  layout.tsx                 # Root: fonts, metadata, globals
  globals.css                # Design tokens (Signal Teal)
  (marketing)/               # Public conversion surfaces
    layout.tsx
    page.tsx                 # Landing
  (auth)/                    # Unauthenticated auth flows
    layout.tsx
    login/page.tsx
    signup/page.tsx
    callback/route.ts        # OAuth / magic-link callback
  (onboarding)/              # first_login === true only
    layout.tsx
    onboarding/page.tsx      # /onboarding
  (app)/                     # Authenticated product shell
    layout.tsx
    chat/page.tsx            # Primary home post-onboarding
    dashboard/page.tsx
    billing/page.tsx
  api/
    chat/route.ts
    billing/…                # Razorpay checkout, verify, portal
    webhooks/razorpay/route.ts

lib/
  ai/
    provider.ts              # AI_PROVIDER / AI_MODEL swap (Gemini | Groq)
    expert-context.ts        # EXPERT_CONTEXT insertion point
    prompts.ts               # System prompt assembly
  supabase/
    client.ts
    server.ts
    middleware.ts
  razorpay/
    client.ts
    plans.ts                 # Placeholder: starter | growth | scale
  types/
    onboarding.ts
    artifacts.ts
    billing.ts

components/
  ui/                        # shadcn primitives (themed)
  marketing/
  onboarding/
  chat/
  dashboard/
  billing/

supabase/
  migrations/                # SQL migrations

middleware.ts                # Auth + first_login + subscription gates
```

### Routing conventions

- Post-onboarding home: **`/(app)/chat`** (dashboard is adjacent, live-updating).
- `first_login === true` → force `/onboarding` before chat/dashboard.
- Subsequent logins → chat.
- Premium features: server-side subscription checks + middleware — never client-only.

---

## AI layer

```ts
// Env (see .env.example)
AI_PROVIDER=gemini | groq
AI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash   // or groq model id
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
```

- Use Vercel AI SDK only. Provider selection in `lib/ai/provider.ts`.
- Swapping providers must not require changes outside `provider.ts` + env.
- System prompt = advisor persona + onboarding JSON + `EXPERT_CONTEXT` + history.
- `EXPERT_CONTEXT` lives in `lib/ai/expert-context.ts` — placeholder topics
  (business-model, traction-signals, deal-structure, red-flags). Model reasons
  from this material in its own words; never quotes it verbatim to the user.

---

## Auth & data

- Supabase Auth: email/password, magic link, Google OAuth.
- Profiles table includes `first_login: boolean` (true on signup).
- Onboarding answers: structured JSON keyed by question id.
- Artifacts: typed JSON (chart-ready), rendered client-side with Recharts.

---

## Billing (Razorpay)

Placeholder plan ids: `starter` | `growth` | `scale` (names/limits TBD).

Implement (scaffold → flesh out in billing step): Checkout, subscription where
supported, payment verification, secure webhooks, upgrade/downgrade/cancel,
success/failure handling. Persist status, plan, renewal dates, transaction
history in Supabase.

---

## Coding standards

- Strict TypeScript; no `any` unless justified with a comment.
- Prefer Server Components; `"use client"` only when needed.
- Colocate feature components under `components/<feature>/`.
- Shared types in `lib/types/`.
- Env vars: never commit secrets; document in `.env.example`.
- Do not add markdown docs unless asked.

---

## Incremental build order (confirm before advancing)

1. ✅ `.cursorrules` + scaffold + route groups + tokens
2. Landing page
3. Auth + `first_login`
4. Onboarding (structure → taste → motion)
5. Chat + onboarding context + placeholder system prompt
6. Dashboard visual analytics per artifact
7. Pricing UI + Razorpay scaffold
